title: Activate a vocabulary
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

A vocabulary is a set of markers grouped together. Markers only fire in tiddlers where their vocabulary is active. Two ways to activate:

!! Type field

Set the tiddler's `type` to include a `;vocab=` parameter listing one or more vocabulary names:

```
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Markdown
```

Default is implicit when no `;vocab=` parameter is present, so a plain `text/vnd.tiddlywiki` tiddler already has [[vocab/default]] active. Add other vocabularies by name (the name is the vocab meta's caption, e.g. `Markdown` resolves to `vocab/markdown`).

[[Example - Markdown]] uses `type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Markdown` to activate just the Markdown vocab without Default.

!! `\importcustom` pragma

Activate by filter at the top of a tiddler:

```
\importcustom [tag[vocab/color-boxes]]
```

Whatever the filter returns is activated for that tiddler only. The pragma works for both marker tiddlers (modern) and `\custom` pragma tiddlers (legacy bridge).

